course: dictionary
lesson: 14288
title: Notification: the message that tells you
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A notification is a short message or alert that pops up on a phone, tablet or computer to tell you something has happened. «My tablet made a ping: I got a notification that my friend had sent a photo.» The message tells you the news so you do not have to go and look for it.
explain: Use the words around the word to work out its meaning. «I got a notification that my game had updated.» The word updated is a clue: something new has happened, and the notification tells you about it. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? A message or alert fits, so that is what notification means.
explain: The word also has a more formal meaning. «The school sent a written notification about the change to our trip.» Here a notification is an official letter or message that tells people about a change. Both meanings are about telling someone that something has happened.
fact: A notification is a message or alert that tells you something has happened.
fact: «Notification» comes from the verb «notify», which means to tell someone.
fact: On phones and tablets, notifications can show new messages, likes and updates.
fact: Formal meaning: an official telling of something, or the letter that does it, such as «a written notification».
fact: Online safety: turn off notifications at bedtime to help you sleep, and never tap a link in a notification from a stranger.
exercise: «My tablet made a ping: a new notification had arrived.» What is a notification? | *A message or alert telling you something has happened | A game you play with friends | A type of bedtime drink | A tablet that has broken
exercise: «Turn off notifications before bed so you can sleep.» Why might this help? | *Alerts will not wake you up or keep you awake | Notifications make your bed warmer | Notifications make the room brighter | You have to read every one before you can sleep
exercise: «The school sent a written notification about the change to our trip.» What does notification mean here? | A type of bag for school books | *An official letter or message telling people about a change | A ring on a finger | A phone game with lots of levels
test: «The notification said my friend had posted a photo.» What does notification mean here? | A friend who posts pictures | *A message or alert on my phone | A photo of my friend | A walk in the park
test: The noun notification comes from which verb? | note | *notify | number | nation
exam: Which sentence uses notification correctly? | «I ate a notification for my lunch.» | «The notification ran around the garden.» | «My notification is a blue woolly jumper.» | *«I turned off my phone notifications so I could sleep.»
